                testing, and standards work through shipment in Chromium 141.
              </li>
              <li>
                Implemented and enabled <code>aria-actions</code> by default in Chromium across
                Windows UI Automation, IAccessible2, and macOS accessibility APIs, with platform
                safeguards, IDL reflection, and web-platform test coverage.
              </li>
              <li>
                Delivered MathML-for-UIA in Chromium and owned the Narrator UIA TextPattern
                scenario, landing UIA custom properties plus fixes for format boundaries, newline
                geometry, and text-range alignment.
              </li>
              <li>
                Represent Microsoft in ARIA, Open UI, WHATWG, and interoperability initiatives;
                align browser vendors, assistive-technology partners, and web developers around
                practical, accessible platform behavior.
              </li>
              <li>
                Serve as a Chromium Accessibility owner and high-volume reviewer, resolving
                release-blocking crashes, security issues, compliance defects, and complex
                cross-product regressions while mentoring engineers in the codebase.
              </li>
            </ul>
